00:14:26,860 --> 00:14:30,660
All right, well, I mean, what can you do? If you lost it, you lost it.

246
00:14:30,820 --> 00:14:33,200
I'll replace it, I promise. I feel so terrible.

247
00:14:33,370 --> 00:14:35,490
That's fine. You didn't do it on purpose.

248
00:14:35,660 --> 00:14:36,870
- No.     - Oh.

249
00:14:37,040 --> 00:14:39,000
Look at you. Come here.

250
00:14:39,160 --> 00:14:40,710
Aw.

251
00:14:41,580 --> 00:14:44,960
- You feel better? Ha, ha.     - Yeah. You're the best.

252
00:14:45,380 --> 00:14:47,380
Okay, wait a minute.

253
00:14:48,340 --> 00:14:50,220
Wait a minute, I can't do this.

254
00:14:50,380 --> 00:14:52,720
Listen, honey, it's not Phoebe's fault.

255
00:14:52,930 --> 00:14:54,680
She lent me the earrings.

256
00:14:54,890 --> 00:14:58,430
I lost it. I'm so sorry, honey. I feel terrible too.

257
00:14:59,980 --> 00:15:02,400
That is exactly why I do not lend you stuff!

258
00:15:04,650 --> 00:15:07,650
First it's my jewelry. If it's not that, it's my sweater.

259
00:15:07,860 --> 00:15:10,190
And if it's not my sweater, it's my sunglasses.

260
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:12,360
- Your sunglasses?     - Yes.

261
00:15:12,530 --> 00:15:13,990
Oh, right.

262
00:15:15,370 --> 00:15:18,120
- Pizza.     - Mine, mine, mine!

263
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:20,750
Okay, here goes.

264
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:24,170
Prepare yourselves for some class-A flirting.

265
00:15:24,380 --> 00:15:26,090
Okay, hold on.

266
00:15:26,550 --> 00:15:27,630
Okay.

267
00:15:29,420 --> 00:15:33,470
If you really like this girl, I don't think flirting is the right way...

268
00:15:33,680 --> 00:15:35,260
Ah! Ah! Ah!

269
00:15:36,100 --> 00:15:37,220
You'll see.

270
00:15:37,390 --> 00:15:38,770
Okay.

271
00:15:40,810 --> 00:15:42,600
Oh, what's her name?

272
00:15:42,810 --> 00:15:43,940
Caitlin!

273
00:15:44,100 --> 00:15:46,110
Caitlin.

274
00:15:52,360 --> 00:15:53,490
Hey.

275
00:15:53,660 --> 00:15:56,200
Oh, we can't keep eating like this. Ha, ha.

276
00:15:58,490 --> 00:16:00,830
Heh. It's, uh, $12.50.

277
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:02,620
Okay, um...

278
00:16:03,540 --> 00:16:04,750
So...

279
00:16:06,840 --> 00:16:11,550
Do you make the pizzas in one of those, uh, wood-burning ovens?

280
00:16:13,130 --> 00:16:16,010
No, actually, I think they're gas.

281
00:16:16,220 --> 00:16:18,600
Gas? Wow, ha, ha.

282
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:21,640
Intense.

283
00:16:23,270 --> 00:16:26,810
If this is the way all the Gellers flirt, we don't have a problem.

284
00:16:28,190 --> 00:16:29,650
Hey, uh...

285
00:16:29,820 --> 00:16:32,400
You know that smell gas has?

286
00:16:37,240 --> 00:16:38,280
Yeah.

287
00:16:38,450 --> 00:16:40,330
They put that in.

288
00:16:41,040 --> 00:16:42,120
What?

289
00:16:42,330 --> 00:16:44,370
The gas is odorless.

290
00:16:44,540 --> 00:16:49,460
But they add the smell so you know when there's a leak.

291
00:16:51,130 --> 00:16:52,380
Well, okay.

292
00:16:54,630 --> 00:16:57,430
A lot of other gas smells.

293
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:04,390
Oh, the humanity.

294
00:17:07,730 --> 00:17:10,900
Methane smells...

295
00:17:11,730 --> 00:17:15,150
You know what? Um, actually, I really should go.

296
00:17:15,360 --> 00:17:18,320
- Oh, but I haven't paid you yet.     - That's okay.

297
00:17:18,530 --> 00:17:21,580
You guys have ordered so many that this one's on me.

298
00:17:22,790 --> 00:17:23,950
Last I heard...

299
00:17:24,120 --> 00:17:27,830
...the cops had over 600 reported missing women still.

300
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:29,040
Six hundred.
600

301
00:17:29,210 --> 00:17:33,300
Was I talking to her about gas?

302
00:17:34,590 --> 00:17:36,920
More so than anything else.

303
00:17:38,590 --> 00:17:41,350
I found it interesting.

304
00:17:43,770 --> 00:17:44,810
I'm sorry.

305
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:47,140
Hey, hey. Don't worry about it.

306
00:17:47,390 --> 00:17:51,810
In nine years, she and I will be right there! Ha, ha.

307
00:17:57,200 --> 00:18:00,740
Okay. Well, I'm gonna clear out some of these boxes.

308
00:18:07,250 --> 00:18:08,460
- Ross?     - Yeah?

309
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:11,210
What else do they add smell to?

310
00:18:15,630 --> 00:18:17,880
Caitlin! Caitlin! Hi.

311
00:18:18,050 --> 00:18:20,340
Hi, I'm Rachel. Oh.

312
00:18:20,550 --> 00:18:22,470
From upstairs, people with all the pizza.

313
00:18:22,640 --> 00:18:24,140
Oh, was there a problem?

314
00:18:24,350 --> 00:18:26,350
No, they're fine. Great pizza.

315
00:18:26,520 --> 00:18:29,520
But, actually, um, my friend Ross...

316
00:18:29,690 --> 00:18:33,560
...he just gets really nervous when he's flirting.

317
00:18:33,980 --> 00:18:36,610
Oh, my God! That was flirting?

318
00:18:36,780 --> 00:18:38,240
- Yeah.     - Wow.

319
00:18:38,490 --> 00:18:40,280
I know, I know.

320
00:18:40,450 --> 00:18:43,700
I'm telling you, once you get past that part...

321
00:18:43,910 --> 00:18:46,330
...where it just feels like you wanna die...

322
00:18:46,580 --> 00:18:48,500
...he's a really good person.

323
00:18:48,660 --> 00:18:51,290
- The guy with the gas?     - Yeah.

324
00:18:51,500 --> 00:18:54,590
I'm telling you, he's really sweet and really funny...

325
00:18:54,750 --> 00:18:57,050
...and he's just, oh, got a good heart.

326
00:18:57,260 --> 00:19:01,340
- And besides, I think he really likes you.     - Really?

327
00:19:01,550 --> 00:19:05,510
Well, we have seven people and 10 pizzas. What do you think?

328
00:19:05,720 --> 00:19:08,520
I thought Joey was there.

329
00:19:11,020 --> 00:19:13,440
You've got till Monday. Then I move to dismiss.

330
00:19:16,360 --> 00:19:17,400
Hey, Ross?

331
00:19:18,320 --> 00:19:20,990
Um, I just ran into Caitlin in the hallway.

332
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:24,990
Uh, you must be getting better at this flirting stuff than I thought. Ha, ha.

333
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:26,580
- What?     - I don't get it...

334
00:19:26,740 --> 00:19:29,540
...but she wanted me to give you her phone number.

335
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:31,160
Oh.

336
00:19:34,460 --> 00:19:36,460
And she just gave you this?

337
00:19:36,630 --> 00:19:38,000
Yeah.

338
00:19:39,840 --> 00:19:43,430
Rach, thanks. But I don't need you doing me any favors.

339
00:19:43,590 --> 00:19:46,100
I didn't. I didn't. She thought you were cute.

340
00:19:47,470 --> 00:19:48,680
Well, that I can believe.

341
00:19:48,850 --> 00:19:50,730
Yeah.

342
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:53,980
Hey, is the show still on?

343
00:19:54,190 --> 00:19:55,520
Almost over, man.

344
00:19:55,690 --> 00:19:57,060
Hey, Nonnie.

345
00:19:57,230 --> 00:19:58,520
Oh! Is that the Pope?

346
00:19:58,690 --> 00:19:59,820
Hey.

347
00:20:02,110 --> 00:20:03,950
Why am I looking?

348
00:20:04,410 --> 00:20:06,620
Oh, Nonnie, here I am! This is my big scene.

349
00:20:07,240 --> 00:20:09,160
All right, back off!

350
00:20:11,040 --> 00:20:12,910
I got a gun!

351
00:20:13,370 --> 00:20:14,830
I'm not afraid to use it.

352
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:16,080
Oh, Joey.

353
00:20:16,250 --> 00:20:17,710
That's right, Nonnie.

354
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:20,460
You couldn't have at least changed your shirt?

355
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:24,720
Now, I want a suitcase filled with $100,000...

356
00:20:26,090 --> 00:20:27,760
Shh! Shoo, shoo!

357
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:31,180
Filled with $100,000 in small bills.

358
00:20:31,350 --> 00:20:33,770
And if I don't get... Shoo!

359
00:20:34,190 --> 00:20:36,230
And if I don't get it...

360
00:20:37,690 --> 00:20:39,270
...I'm gonna shoot this duck!

361
00:20:39,690 --> 00:20:41,690
Oh, no!

362
00:20:42,570 --> 00:20:44,700
I'm coming out!

363
00:20:52,250 --> 00:20:54,160
And she's supposed to buy this?

364
00:20:58,380 --> 00:21:01,500
Ground control to Major Tom

365
00:21:03,630 --> 00:21:05,630
Commencing countdown

366
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:07,720
Engines

367
00:21:08,180 --> 00:21:09,850
On

368
00:21:16,020 --> 00:21:18,850
That's, uh, scenes from next week's show. Next week.

369
00:21:20,610 --> 00:21:22,940
I am definitely gonna watch that.

370
00:21:28,620 --> 00:21:30,450
What about these? Do these look the same?

371
00:21:30,660 --> 00:21:32,700
- Definitely.     - Not as each other.

372
00:21:32,870 --> 00:21:34,660
Oh, then, no.

373
00:21:37,290 --> 00:21:39,250
- Hey, you ready?     - Hi. Yeah.

374
00:21:39,500 --> 00:21:40,790
- You look amazing.     - Aw.

375
00:21:40,960 --> 00:21:42,750
I'm the luckiest man in the world.

376
00:21:42,920 --> 00:21:45,590
- Oh, you're about to get a little luckier.     - Mm-hm.

377
00:21:45,760 --> 00:21:48,470
- Let me see the earrings.     - Oh, right, the earrings.

378
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:50,220
They look great.

379
00:21:50,390 --> 00:21:52,890
Does your boyfriend have the best taste or what?

380
00:21:54,470 --> 00:21:56,140
My boyfriend really does have great taste.

381
00:22:01,940 --> 00:22:03,980
- Thanks for picking out the earrings.     - Mm-hm.

